  "notes": "セール is a loanword from English \"sale,\" referring to discount sales or promotional events.\n\nCommon expressions:\n- セール{中|ちゅう} (on sale, during the sale)\n- セールを{行|おこな}う (to hold a sale)\n- {夏|なつ}のセール / {冬|ふゆ}のセール (summer/winter sale)\n- タイムセール (time-limited sale)\n- {閉店|へいてん}セール (closing sale)\n- {決算|けっさん}セール (end-of-fiscal-year sale)\n\nNote: In Japanese, セール specifically means a discount sale, not the general act of selling (which is {販売|はんばい}).\n\nRelated terms:\n- バーゲン (bargain sale)\n- {安売|やすう}り (selling at a discount)\n- {特売|とくばい} (special sale)",
